  "title": "Delhi Building Collapse and Government Response",
  "summary": "A five-storey building in Delhi's Satya Niketan area collapsed, resulting in one death and several trapped individuals. The collapse was attributed to construction practices and was reported by officials who emphasized the need for immediate rescue efforts and coordination with local authorities.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "A five-storey building near Delhi University's south campus collapsed, leaving one dead and several trapped.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Officials said the building was vacated as a precautionary measure, and the local administration and NDRF are conducting rescue operations.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Amit Shah, Union Home Minister, spoke with Delhi Chief Minister Rekha Gupta and other officials after the collapse, highlighting the need for medical assistance and coordination.",
